{"core": "Compassion feels what another feels and moves toward them. In Nurturing, it works on the ground that feeds — the slow, steady provision that keeps things alive before they are strong enough to ask. Overdone, the feeling outruns the feeding: every pull of need draws an immediate pour, and the ground gives faster than it refills. What was soil becomes a drain.", "sheetLine": "Every pull of need draws an immediate pour; the ground runs dry."}
